description: Double-entry accounting rules
alwaysApply: false
globs: "apps/api/**/accounting/**/*.{ts,sql},apps/api/**/journal/**/*.{ts,sql},apps/api/**/ledger/**/*.{ts,sql},apps/api/**/invoice/**/*.{ts,sql}"
Accounting Rules

The accounting system uses double-entry bookkeeping.

Every journal entry must balance:

Debit total = Credit total

Accounting must be auditable.

Do not delete historical financial transactions.

Corrections should use reversal/adjustment mechanisms.

Before changing accounting:

Read docs/ACCOUNTING.md.
Identify the business event.
Identify affected accounts.
Define debit and credit behavior.
Implement through accounting services.
Add tests.
Verify that entries balance.

Potential accounting events include:

sales
refunds
purchases
inventory
COGS
payment gateway fees
shipping revenue
shipping expense
reseller commissions
taxes
adjustments

Never invent accounting treatment.

If the accounting treatment is unclear, stop and ask for clarification.

Never use floating-point arithmetic for financial calculations.